IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-duties`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2020 (WA) and the Work Health and Safety (General) Regulations 2022, ss 5, 7, 8, 17, 19-21, 27-39, 47, 84-88, 104-115, 267, 272, 273; regs 35, 36, 40, 699 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The regulations used are the deposited Work Health and Safety (General) Regulations
-- 2022 (mrdoc 49725).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_work-health-and-safety-act-2020_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts used (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake and -daniel, facts.json): Jarrah Legal Technologies
-- takes on its first three employees on 1 June 2031 (d044), asked from an employee's seat. Jake, a security officer
-- employed by Sentinel Security Services Pty Ltd and posted to the tower where Jarrah is a tenant, falls on a wet
-- stairwell on patrol on 5 October 2053, is off eleven weeks and is assessed at 14% whole person impairment (k085; d080
-- from the tenant's side). The scenarios do not say who contracted Sentinel, who controls the stairwell, what made it
-- wet, what treatment Jake needed or what a doctor certified: those facts are ILLUSTRATIVE, and where the answer turns
-- on them both answers are asserted. The building manager is an illustrative actor the scenarios do not name.

§ `fixtures`

`Sentinel Security Services, Jake's employer` MEANS `The other person` WITH
